# Mutinous Massacre {3}{B}{B}{R}{R}: "Choose odd or even. Destroy each creature with mana value of the chosen quality. Then gain control of all creatures until end of turn. Untap
# them. They gain haste until end of turn." Bot1's Memnite (0, even) attacks on turn 3 and so is tapped; Bot2 has a Haywire Mite (1) and an Ornithopter (0). Choosing Odd destroys the
# Mite, while it is still Bot2's, so Bot2 gains the 2 life (CR 701.8, 603.10a) - taking it first would have gained them for Bot1. Then Bot1 gains control of every creature left, its own
# Memnite included (untapped now, with haste) and Bot2's Ornithopter. At the end of the turn Bot2 has the Ornithopter back, without haste (CR 514.2); Memnite stays Bot1's.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Memnite
Mutinous Massacre
Island x13

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Haywire Mite
Ornithopter
Island x17

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Memnite.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Haywire Mite.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Memnite > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#1.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby#2.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = true
Bot1.Hand.Mutinous Massacre.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Modes(Odd)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Tapped = false
? Bot1.Battlefield.Memnite.Keywords = Haste
? Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying; Haste
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Ruby
? Bot2.Life = 21
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
? Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Memnite; Mox Pearl; Mox Ruby; Mox Ruby; Mox Sapphire
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Ruby; Ornithopter
Bot2.Graveyard = Haywire Mite
Bot1.Graveyard = Mutinous Massacre; Black Lotus
Bot1.Life = 20
Bot2.Life = 21
